{% layout "default" %}

{% block content %}
  <div class="flex flex-col min-w-30 w-full">
    {% render "poll-title"
      , title: poll.title
      , remaining: null %}
    <p>The poll is ended. Here's how each item was classified.</p>

    <div class="flex flex-col gap-3 px-6 py-4 my-0 w-full text-zinc-200 bg-sky-700 rounded-xl">
      {% for entry in results.features %}
        <div class="py-1 w-full border-b border-zinc-50 border-opacity-15 last:border-b-0">
          <div class="flex flex-row flex-nowrap items-center gap-2">
            <span class="text-lg font-bold text-zinc-100">{{ entry.name | escape }}</span>
            <span class="ml-auto px-2 py-0.5 rounded-md text-sm font-bold whitespace-nowrap
              {% case entry.category %}
                {% when 'M' %}bg-red-500 text-white
                {% when 'O' %}bg-orange-500 text-white
                {% when 'A' %}bg-emerald-500 text-white
                {% when 'I' %}bg-zinc-500 text-white
                {% when 'R' %}bg-purple-600 text-white
                {% else %}bg-zinc-700 text-zinc-300
              {% endcase %}">{{ entry.category_name | escape }}</span>
          </div>
          <div class="flex flex-row flex-wrap gap-x-4 gap-y-1 mt-1 text-sm">
            <span title="Satisfaction if present">Better: <b>{{ entry.better | times: 100 | round }}%</b></span>
            <span title="Dissatisfaction if absent">Worse: <b>{{ entry.worse | times: 100 | round }}%</b></span>
            <span class="ml-auto text-zinc-300 whitespace-nowrap" title="Must-be / Performance / Attractive / Indifferent / Reverse / Questionable">
              M {{ entry.counts.M }} · O {{ entry.counts.O }} · A {{ entry.counts.A }} · I {{ entry.counts.I }} · R {{ entry.counts.R }} · Q {{ entry.counts.Q }}
            </span>
          </div>
        </div>
      {% endfor %}
      <div class="my-2">Total participants: {{ results.total_voters | escape }}</div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <small class="inline-block mt-4">
    Each answer pair is classified with the Kano evaluation table; an item's category is the most common classification (ties go to Must-be, then Performance, Attractive, Indifferent, Reverse, Questionable).
    <b>Must-be</b>: expected, its absence causes dissatisfaction.
    <b>Performance</b>: more is better, less is worse.
    <b>Attractive</b>: delights when present, not missed when absent.
    <b>Indifferent</b>: viewers don't care either way.
    <b>Reverse</b>: viewers would rather not have it.
    <b>Questionable</b>: contradictory answers.
    <b>Better</b> is the share of A+O among non-questionable, non-reverse answers (how much satisfaction rises if present); <b>Worse</b> is the share of O+M (how much satisfaction falls if absent).
  </small>
</div>{% endblock %}
